  "task": "X45 h=4 common-gcd orbit compression",
  "theorem": "For n=2^s and p == 1 mod n, the degree of gcd(Phi_n,E1,E2,E3) for an h=4 signed exponent pattern is invariant under common translation, odd-unit dilation, and side swap.  Translation multiplies E_r by X^(rd), which is coprime to Phi_n; unit dilation composes E_r with X^u and permutes primitive n-th roots; swapping sides multiplies E_r by -1.  Thus a row certifier may check one canonical affine-orbit representative."
